%% Playback flow with HLS over CDN
%% Note: only the manifest fetch hits your services; segments stream straight from CDN

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Cl as Client (player)
    participant API as API gateway
    participant Pb as Playback service
    participant R as Redis (hot meta)
    participant Pg as Postgres
    participant CDN as CDN edge POP
    participant S3 as S3 origin (us-east + eu-west)
    participant Bus as Kafka (analytics)
    participant CH as ClickHouse

    Cl->>API: GET /tracks/abc/manifest (JWT)
    API->>Pb: forward (with user_id, region)
    Pb->>R: GET track:abc
    alt cache hit
        R-->>Pb: {hls_manifest_url, available_regions, ...}
    else cache miss
        Pb->>Pg: SELECT track WHERE id=abc
        Pg-->>Pb: row
        Pb->>R: SETEX 5min
    end
    Pb->>Pb: check region + tier + license
    Pb-->>Cl: 302 → signed CDN URL (15-min expiry)

    Note over Cl,CDN: Audio path bypasses your services entirely
    Cl->>CDN: GET /track/abc/v1/aac128/playlist.m3u8
    alt edge cache hit (~99% on hot tracks)
        CDN-->>Cl: m3u8
    else miss
        CDN->>S3: origin pull
        S3-->>CDN: m3u8
        CDN-->>Cl: m3u8 (filled cache)
    end

    loop For each segment (ABR may switch bitrate)
        Cl->>CDN: GET /track/abc/v1/aac128/seg-NNN.aac
        CDN-->>Cl: bytes (range-friendly, immutable, 30d cache)
    end

    Cl-)API: POST /plays (fire-and-forget, 202)
    API->>Bus: emit play_started event
    Bus->>CH: append (async)
